{% template gt_item %}{% comment %}
One activity row, like STRMNL's: framework item with its meta bar; the sport
icon sits inline in the title at the title's size.
Args: c, name, km, dur, el, t, now, off, noff.
{% endcomment %}<div class="item item--emphasis-2">
  <div class="meta"></div>
  <div class="content gt-clip">
    {%- assign name_len = name | size %}
    <span class="title{% if name_len > 16 %} title--small{% endif %} gt-clip">{% render "gt_sym", n: c, size: "1em" %}<span class="gt-name">{{ name }}</span></span>
    <span class="description gt-clip">{% if km > 0 %}{{ km }} km / {% endif %}{{ dur }}{% if el > 0 %} / {{ el }} m{% endif %}</span>
    <div class="flex gap--small"><span class="label label--small label--underline">{% render "gt_when", t: t, now: now, off: off, noff: noff %}</span></div>
  </div>
</div>{% endtemplate %}
{% template gt_meter %}{% comment %}
A 0-100 score as a framework progress bar with an icon.
Args: n (icon), l (label), v (value or blank), note (text after the value),
sz (progress-bar size: large by default, base for tight spaces).
{% endcomment %}<div class="flex gt-meter" style="align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
  {% render "gt_sym", n: n, size: 26 %}
  <div class="progress-bar progress-bar--{{ sz | default: 'large' }}" style="flex: 1;">
    <div class="content">
      <span class="label">{{ l }}</span>
      <span class="label gt-meter-val">{% if note != blank %}<span class="gt-note">{{ note }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="value value--xsmall value--tnums">{% if v == blank %}-{% else %}{{ v }}{% endif %}</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: {% if v == blank %}0{% else %}{{ v | at_most: 100 }}{% endif %}%"></div></div>
  </div>
</div>{% endtemplate %}
{% template gt_cmp %}{% comment %}
One sport's week: this week (solid) next to last week (framework dither),
km under each bar, change against last week at the same point in the week.
Args: c (sport), tw, lw (km), ltd (last week's km by now), h (bar area px).
{% endcomment %}{%- liquid
  assign top = tw | at_least: lw | at_least: 0.1
  assign th = tw | times: h | divided_by: top | round
  assign lh = lw | times: h | divided_by: top | round
  if ltd > 0
    assign pct = tw | minus: ltd | times: 100.0 | divided_by: ltd | round
    if pct > 0
      assign change = "+" | append: pct | append: "%"
    else
      assign change = pct | append: "%"
    endif
  elsif tw > 0
    assign change = "new"
  else
    assign change = ""
  endif
-%}
<div class="gt-cmp">
  <div class="flex" style="align-items: center; gap: 6px; justify-content: center;">{% render "gt_sym", n: c, size: 22 %}<span class="title title--small">{{ change }}</span></div>
  <div class="gt-cmp-bars" style="height: {{ h }}px;">
    <div class="gt-cmp-bar bg--black" style="height: {{ th }}px;"></div>
    <div class="gt-cmp-bar bg--gray-45" style="height: {{ lh }}px;"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="gt-cmp-vals"><span class="label label--small">{{ tw }} km</span><span class="label label--small">{{ lw }} km</span></div>
</div>{% endtemplate %}
{% template gt_bar %}{% comment %}
Title bar: Garmin's logo with "Connect", the screen name on the right.
Args: instance.
{% endcomment %}<div class="title_bar">
  <span class="gt-brand">{% render "gt_logo", h: 16 %}</span>
  <span class="title">Connect</span>
  <span class="instance">{{ instance }}</span>
</div>{% endtemplate %}
{% template gt_stat %}{% comment %}
One stat: framework item with meta bar, stat icon, big value and label.
Args: n (icon), v (value), u (unit), l (label), size (value size), icon (px).
{% endcomment %}<div class="item item--emphasis-2">
  <div class="meta"></div>
  <div class="icon">{% render "gt_sym", n: n, size: icon %}</div>
  <div class="content">
    <span class="value value--{{ size | default: 'small' }} value--tnums gt-nowrap">{% if v == blank %}-{% else %}{{ v }}{% if u != blank %}<span class="gt-unit">{{ u }}</span>{% endif %}{% endif %}</span>
    <span class="label label--small gt-nowrap">{{ l }}</span>
  </div>
</div>{% endtemplate %}
{% template gt_route %}{% comment %}
The route as an SVG line, scaled to its box. Args: r (path), rb ([w, h, end x,
end y]), w (stroke px at full size; dots scale with it).
{% endcomment %}{%- liquid
  assign pad = w | times: 3
  assign vb_w = rb[0] | plus: pad | plus: pad
  assign vb_h = rb[1] | plus: pad | plus: pad
  assign x0 = r | remove_first: "M" | split: "l" | first | split: " " | first
  assign y0 = r | remove_first: "M" | split: "l" | first | split: " " | last
  assign dot = w | times: 1.6 | round
  assign sq = w | times: 2.8 | round
  assign half = sq | divided_by: 2
  assign ex = rb[2] | minus: half
  assign ey = rb[3] | minus: half
-%}
<svg viewBox="-{{ pad }} -{{ pad }} {{ vb_w }} {{ vb_h }}" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
  <path class="gt-route" d="{{ r }}" style="stroke-width: {{ w }}px;"/>
  <circle cx="{{ x0 }}" cy="{{ y0 }}" r="{{ dot }}" fill="#fff" stroke="#000" stroke-width="{{ w | times: 0.8 }}"/>
  <rect x="{{ ex }}" y="{{ ey }}" width="{{ sq }}" height="{{ sq }}" fill="#000"/>
</svg>{% endtemplate %}
{% template gt_basemap %}{% comment %}
The route over OpenStreetMap tiles with the framework's map engine (TRMNLMaps
+ MapLibre from TRMNL's mirror; tiles from maps.trmnl.com). Renders on
TRMNL's server; an offline render shows an empty map.
Args: el (unique element id), poly (encoded polyline), preset (streets | minimal).
{% endcomment %}
{%- comment %} The polyline travels in an HTML attribute, read back with
getAttribute: no JavaScript string escaping (it may contain backslashes). {% endcomment %}
<div id="{{ el }}" class="map" data-poly="{{ poly | escape }}"></div>
<link href="https://trmnl.com/js/maplibre-gl/5.24.0/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://trmnl.com/js/maplibre-gl/5.24.0/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
<script>
(function () {
  var el = "{{ el }}", preset = "{{ preset }}";
  var poly = document.getElementById(el).getAttribute("data-poly") || "";
  function whenReady(cb) {
    var tries = 0;
    (function attempt() {
      if (window.TRMNLMaps && window.maplibregl) return cb();
      if (++tries > 200) return;
      setTimeout(attempt, 50);
    })();
  }
  // Build once the whole page is parsed: the map box gets its final size
  // only after the markup below it exists.
  function onParsed(cb) {
    if (document.readyState === "loading") document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", cb);
    else cb();
  }
  onParsed(function () { whenReady(function () {
    var route = TRMNLMaps.decodePolyline(poly);
    if (route.length < 2) return;
    TRMNLMaps.watch(el, function () {
      // Keep the ground quiet so the track reads: no building footprints,
      // only major place names ("streets"), or coast, water and main roads
      // only ("simple" = the outline preset).
      var opts = preset === "minimal"
        ? { el: el, preset: "outline", labels: "major" }
        : { el: el, preset: "minimal", labels: "major", buildings: false };
      var map = new maplibregl.Map(TRMNLMaps.options(opts));
      map.on("load", function () {
        // Re-measure the box and frame the route for its final size.
        map.resize();
        TRMNLMaps.fit(map, route, { padding: TRMNLPaint.px(16, { el: el }), maxZoom: 15 });
        TRMNLMaps.route(map, route, { el: el, width: 7 });
        TRMNLMaps.dot(map, route[0], { el: el, id: "start", hollow: true, radius: 9 });
        TRMNLMaps.dot(map, route[route.length - 1], { el: el, id: "end", radius: 9 });
      });
      TRMNLMaps.fit(map, route, { padding: TRMNLPaint.px(16, { el: el }), maxZoom: 15 });
      return map;
    });
  }); });
})();
</script>{% endtemplate %}
{% liquid
  assign off = trmnl.user.utc_offset | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign now = trmnl.system.timestamp_utc | default: ts | plus: 0
  assign cf = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values
  assign screen = cf.screen | default: "latest"
  assign map_mode = cf.map | default: "route"
  assign stale_h = cf.stale_hours | default: 4 | plus: 0
  assign stale_s = stale_h | times: 3600
  assign age = now | minus: ts
  assign stale = false
  if ts == blank or age > stale_s
    assign stale = true
  endif
  assign auth_err = false
  if err == "auth"
    assign auth_err = true
  endif
  assign ts_hh = ts | plus: off | modulo: 86400 | divided_by: 3600 | plus: 100 | append: "" | slice: 1, 2
  assign ts_mi = ts | plus: off | modulo: 3600 | divided_by: 60 | plus: 100 | append: "" | slice: 1, 2
  assign age_h = age | divided_by: 3600
  case screen
  when "splits"
    assign screen_name = "Splits"
  when "heart"
    assign screen_name = "Heart rate"
  when "week"
    assign screen_name = "Week"
  when "recovery"
    assign screen_name = "Recovery"
  else
    assign screen = "latest"
    assign screen_name = "Latest activity"
  endcase

  # --- latest activity ---------------------------------------------------
  assign has_a = false
  if a.st
    assign has_a = true
  endif
  assign a_km = a.d | default: 0 | divided_by: 1000.0 | round: 1
  if a_km >= 100
    assign a_km = a_km | round
  endif
  assign a_mt = a.mt | default: a.t | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign a_kind = "pace"
  if a.c == "ride"
    assign a_kind = "speed"
  endif
  assign a_rate = ""
  assign a_rate_unit = ""
  if a.d and a.d > 0 and a_mt > 0
    if a_kind == "speed"
      assign a_rate = a.d | times: 3.6 | divided_by: a_mt | round: 1
      assign a_rate_unit = "km/h"
    elsif a.c == "swim"
      assign a_rate_s = a_mt | times: 100.0 | divided_by: a.d | round
      assign a_rate_unit = "/100m"
    else
      assign a_rate_s = a_mt | times: 1000.0 | divided_by: a.d | round
      assign a_rate_unit = "/km"
    endif
  endif
  assign a_off = a.o | default: off
  assign a_has_d = false
  if a.d and a.d > 0
    assign a_has_d = true
  endif
  assign a_climb = false
  if a.c == "hike" or a.c == "walk"
    assign a_climb = true
  endif
  assign a_te = a.te[0] | times: 1.0 | round: 1
  capture a_dur
    render "gt_dur", s: a_mt
  endcapture
  assign a_dur_label = "Moving time"
  if a_climb
    # Hikes and walks carry timer time in a.mt (see normalize.TIMER_SPORTS).
    assign a_dur_label = "Time"
  endif
  assign a_rate_v = "-"
  assign a_rate_label = "Avg pace"
  if a_kind == "speed" and a_rate != ""
    assign a_rate_v = a_rate
    assign a_rate_label = "Avg speed"
  elsif a_rate_s
    capture a_rate_v
      render "gt_pace", p: a_rate_s
    endcapture
  endif
  assign a_sport = a.sp | default: "activity" | replace: "_", " " | capitalize
  assign a_name = a.n | default: a_sport

  # Route: an SVG line (no JS) or, when the setting asks for a map and the
  # payload carries the polyline, the framework's map engine.
  assign show_route = false
  if map_mode != "off" and a.r
    assign show_route = true
  endif
  assign use_basemap = false
  if show_route and a.p
    if map_mode == "streets" or map_mode == "minimal"
      assign use_basemap = true
    endif
  endif
  if a.r
    assign r_x0 = a.r | remove_first: "M" | split: "l" | first | split: " " | first
    assign r_y0 = a.r | remove_first: "M" | split: "l" | first | split: " " | last
  endif

  # HR chart: "min,max,chars", one base64url char per bin (64 levels).
  assign hr_pts = ""
  assign hr_n = 0
  if a.h
    assign hp = a.h | split: ","
    assign hr_lo = hp[0]
    assign hr_hi = hp[1]
    assign hr_chars = hp[2]
    assign hr_n = hr_chars | size
    assign B64 = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_"
    assign last_i = hr_n | minus: 1
    for i in (0..last_i)
      assign ch = hr_chars | slice: i, 1
      assign lev = B64 | split: ch | first | size
      assign y = 63 | minus: lev
      assign hr_pts = hr_pts | append: i | append: "," | append: y | append: " "
    endfor
    assign hr_w = hr_n | minus: 1
    assign hr_mid = hr_lo | plus: hr_hi | divided_by: 2.0 | round
  endif

  # Time in HR zones: seconds -> percent of the total and of the largest zone.
  assign z_total = 0
  assign z_max = 0
  for z in a.z
    assign z_total = z_total | plus: z
    if z > z_max
      assign z_max = z
    endif
  endfor

  # Splits: s per unit (run/hike/walk) or km/h x10 (ride). Taller = faster.
  assign spl_n = 0
  if a.spl
    assign sv = a.spl | split: ","
    assign spl_n = sv | size
    assign best = 0
    assign worst = 0
    assign spl_sum = 0
    for v in sv
      assign x = v | plus: 0
      assign spl_sum = spl_sum | plus: x
      if a.c == "ride"
        if x > best
          assign best = x
        endif
        if worst == 0 or x < worst
          assign worst = x
        endif
      else
        if best == 0 or x < best
          assign best = x
        endif
        if x > worst
          assign worst = x
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    assign spl_avg = spl_sum | times: 1.0 | divided_by: spl_n | round
  endif

  # --- week ------------------------------------------------------------------
  assign days = d14 | default: "" | split: ","
  assign wk_max = 1
  # TRMNL's Liquid does not apply filters inside `for ... in`: build lists first.
  assign wk_keys = "run,ride,hike,lrun,lride,lhike" | split: ","
  assign wk_cats = "run,ride,hike" | split: ","
  assign wk_days = "Mo,Tu,We,Th,Fr,Sa,Su" | split: ","
  # Latest-activity stats in order of interest for the sport. The ones with a
  # value become parallel lists (st_v, st_u, st_l, st_i, st_n entries); each
  # layout shows the first few. "§" separates entries.
  if a_has_d == false
    assign stat_keys = "time,calories,heart,maxhr,load,te" | split: ","
  elsif a_climb
    assign stat_keys = "distance,time,ascent,heart,calories,load,maxhr,rate" | split: ","
  else
    assign stat_keys = "distance,time,rate,heart,ascent,load,maxhr,calories" | split: ","
  endif
  capture load_label
    echo "Load"
    if a.te
      echo " · TE " | append: a_te
    endif
  endcapture
  assign st_v = ""
  assign st_u = ""
  assign st_l = ""
  assign st_i = ""
  assign st_n = 0
  for k in stat_keys
    assign v_ = nil
    case k
    when "distance"
      assign v_ = a_km
      assign u_ = "km"
      assign l_ = "Distance"
      assign i_ = "distance"
    when "time"
      assign v_ = a_dur
      assign u_ = ""
      assign l_ = a_dur_label
      assign i_ = "time"
    when "rate"
      assign v_ = a_rate_v
      assign u_ = a_rate_unit
      assign l_ = a_rate_label
      assign i_ = "speed"
    when "heart"
      assign v_ = a.hr
      assign u_ = "bpm"
      assign l_ = "Avg heart rate"
      assign i_ = "heart"
    when "maxhr"
      assign v_ = a.mx
      assign u_ = "bpm"
      assign l_ = "Max heart rate"
      assign i_ = "heart"
    when "ascent"
      assign v_ = a.el
      assign u_ = "m"
      assign l_ = "Ascent"
      assign i_ = "ascent"
    when "calories"
      assign v_ = a.kc
      assign u_ = "kcal"
      assign l_ = "Calories"
      assign i_ = "calories"
    when "load"
      assign v_ = a.ld
      assign u_ = ""
      assign l_ = load_label
      assign i_ = "load"
    when "te"
      assign v_ = a.te[0]
      assign u_ = ""
      assign l_ = "Aerobic training effect"
      assign i_ = "status"
    endcase
    if v_ != blank and v_ != "-"
      assign st_v = st_v | append: v_ | append: "§"
      assign st_u = st_u | append: u_ | append: "§"
      assign st_l = st_l | append: l_ | append: "§"
      assign st_i = st_i | append: i_ | append: "§"
      assign st_n = st_n | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
  # Ruby's split drops trailing empty strings, so a missing last unit reads as nil.
  assign st_v = st_v | split: "§"
  assign st_u = st_u | split: "§"
  assign st_l = st_l | split: "§"
  assign st_i = st_i | split: "§"
  for k in wk_keys
    assign v = wk[k][0] | default: 0
    if v > wk_max
      assign wk_max = v
    endif
  endfor

  # --- wellness -----------------------------------------------------------
  assign st_name = w.tst | default: "" | replace: "_", " " | downcase | capitalize
  assign hrv_name = w.hrv | default: "" | replace: "_", " " | downcase | capitalize
-%}
<style>
  .gt { height: 100%; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .gt * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  .gt-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; height: 100%; min-height: 0; }
  .gt-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-width: 0; min-height: 0; }
  .gt-sym { display: block; fill: currentColor; flex: none; }
  .title .gt-sym { display: inline-block; vertical-align: -0.12em; margin-right: 0.3em; }
  .gt-logo { display: block; fill: currentColor; }
  .gt-meter-val { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; }
  .gt-brand { display: flex; align-items: center; margin-right: 6px; }
  .gt-cmp { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; min-width: 0; flex: 1 1 0; }
  .gt-cmp-bars { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center; gap: 6px; }
  .gt-cmp-bar { width: 38%; max-width: 40px; border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; }
  .gt-cmp-vals { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 6px; }
